    <statement><p>Evaluate the line integral
<m>\int_C 5 y \, dx + 2 x \, dy</m> where <m>C</m> is the
straight line path from <m>(1,1)</m> to <m>(3, 6)</m>.</p>
<p><m>\int_C 5 y \, dx + 2 x \, dy =</m> <fillin characters="45" name="AnSwEr0001"/></p>
</statement>
    <answer>
      <p>
        <m>5\cdot \left(\frac{6-1}{2}+1\right)\mathopen{}\left(3-1\right)+2\cdot \left(\frac{3-1}{2}+1\right)\mathopen{}\left(6-1\right)</m>
      </p>
    </answer>
    <solution><m>C</m>:
<me>x= 1 + 2 t, \qquad y = 1 + 5 t, \qquad 0\le t \le 1,</me>
so that  <m>dx= 2\, dt</m> and <m>dy = 5\,dt</m>.  Hence
<me>\int_C 5 y \, dx + 2 x \, dy =
\int_0^1 5(1 + 5 t)2\, dt + 2(1 + 2 t)5\, dt =
\int_0^1 20 + 70 t\, dt = 55.</me>



</solution>
